A '''Hiker''' (Japanese: '''やまおとこ''' ''Mountaineer'' and '''やまガール''' ''Mountain Girl'') is a type of [[Pokémon Trainer]] that debuted in the [[Generation I]] games. They typically appear as large, usually bearded men carrying a walking stick and wearing hiking gear. In the following generations, they also carry a large [[bag|backpack]]. In [[Generation IX]], female Hikers were introduced.

They specialize in a combination of {{t|Fighting}}-, {{t|Ground}}-, and {{type|Rock}} Pokémon that are common in mountains and caves, such as {{p|Onix}}, {{p|Machop}}, and {{p|Geodude}}, although not all of them exclusively train those types.

In [[Pokémon: Let's Go, Pikachu! and Let's Go, Eevee!|Let's Go, Pikachu! and Let's Go, Eevee!]], aside from [[Master Trainer]]s, Hikers will award three {{i|Poké Ball}}s along with [[prize money]] upon being defeated.

